Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 22:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Allow shutter sound control for all locales

HyperOS obtains the regulatory region independently from the display locale.
AOSP exposes no equivalent setting, so selecting Japanese also makes the
camera treat the device as a mandatory-shutter-sound market.  That hides the
preference and makes the sound manager ignore its stored value even when the
actual device region does not require it.

Keep the shutter sound policy optional in this AOSP integration.  The common
policy method is shared by preference construction, Settings search and sound
playback, so overriding it both exposes the switch and makes the switch take
effect consistently.
---
 smali_classes4/H7/c.smali | 42 ------------------------------------------
 1 file changed, 42 deletions(-)

